>Has anyone else noticed that the old trick of teleporting around to get
>oneself out of the "Satiated" state is no longer as useful in 3.1.2.
>Seems that teleports now use up spell energy, and you can run out and
>not be able to teleport.
>
>Oh well, I knew they'd find out that hack eventually. It used to be so easy
>to eat all those giants one after the other, too.

I haven't got 3.1.2 yet, but I can think of another possible explanation.
Normally in nethack, hitting ctrl-T will teleport you any way it can.  
If you have the "teleport at will" intrisic, this means do the "teleport
at will".  However, if you don't have "teleport at will", ctrl-T will try
to use the "teleport away" spell cast at yourself.  This would cause you
to lose energy points.
